# KEYS: newsboat

## Navigation

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| **j** / **k** | Move down / up in the list |
| **l** / **Enter** | Open the selected entry or feed |
| **h** / **q** | Back to previous view / Quit current view |
| **Q** | Quit newsboat immediately |
| **J** / **K** | Move to previous / next feed in the list |
| **n** | Jump to the next unread article |
| **N** | Jump to the previous unread article |

---

## Article Management

* **a** - Toggle the selected article's status as Read/Unread.
* **A** - Mark all articles in the current feed as Read.
* **r** - Reload the current feed.
* **R** - Reload all feeds.
* **s** - Save the article to a file.

---

## Link Handling

`newsboat` allows for powerful link manipulation, often extended via custom macros in the configuration file.

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| **U** | Show a list of all URLs within the article |
| **, ,** | Open the main article link with a custom `linkhandler` script |
| **, p** | Pick which external program to open the link with |
| **, v** | Open the video link directly in `mpv` |
| **, w** | Open the link in the `w3m` terminal browser |
| **, c** | Copy the link to the system clipboard |

---

## Configuration & Filters

* **/** - Search for articles.
* **&** - Filter articles by a specific expression.
* **ctrl-p** - Go to previous item.
* **ctrl-n** - Go to next item.

### Essential Files
* **Feeds list:** `~/.newsboat/urls`
* **Configuration:** `~/.newsboat/config`

